Effectiveness of a Counseling Intervention to Increase Vaccination Uptake among Men Who Have Sex with Men during the Mpox Outbreak,"Men who have sex with men (MSM) are disproportionately impacted by sexually transmitted infections (STIs), including HIV and those preventable through vaccination such as mpox, HPV, HAV, and HBV. A retrospective cohort study was conducted to evaluate the effectiveness of counseling provided during mpox vaccination on the uptake of other recommended vaccines (HPV, HAV, and HBV) and to identify associated factors. Relevant covariates such as nationality, age, HIV status, and use of PrEP were retrieved from electronic medical records. Vaccination status data were retrieved from the regional vaccination registry. Of the 330 participants, 98.8% were males and the mean age was 40.6 years (SD: 11.2). Following consultation, a statistically significant increase for both HPV (from 25.8% to 39.1%) and HAV (from 26.7% to 36.1%) was observed (p < 0.001). The multivariate analysis showed a significant negative association between the uptake of HPV and HBV vaccines and foreign nationality (aOR 0.25 (95%CI 0.08–0.69), p = 0.012; and aOR 0.31 (95%CI 0.11–0.81), p = 0.021). The HBV vaccine uptake was negatively associated with increasing age. Our results suggest that tailored counseling can effectively bridge the gap in vaccine acceptance among vulnerable populations, thereby improving overall public health outcomes.","M. Ogliastro, A. Ferrari, L. Sticchi, A. Domnich, Giacomo Zappa, A. Di Biagio, Elvira Massaro, Elisa Giribaldi, A. Orsi",10.3390/vaccines12070751,https://doi.org/10.3390/vaccines12070751,Vaccines,5,2024,yes,"The study population includes individuals with HIV and those using PrEP, meaning it is not exclusively limited to 'healthy' individuals.",no,"The study reports on vaccine uptake for other diseases (HPV, HAV, HBV) but does not report on mpox infection prevention, hospitalization, death, or safety outcomes for the mpox vaccine itself.",yes,The study is described as a retrospective cohort study.,yes,This is a study involving human participants recruited from medical records.,no,The participants were MSM with a mean age of 40.6 years. There is no mention of participants under age 18 or pregnant women.,no,"The participants received the vaccine during the mpox outbreak as adults (mean age 40.6), not during pregnancy, childhood, or adolescence.",yes,The study involves participants receiving the mpox vaccine.,Exclude,"This study focuses on an adult MSM population with a mean age of 40.6 years, failing to include the target populations of children or pregnant women. Additionally, it evaluates the uptake of other vaccines rather than clinical effectiveness or safety outcomes for mpox.","Relevant Outcomes, Target Population, Vaccination Timing",Target Population,0.1,"  - ""nationality, age, HIV status, and use of PrEP were retrieved""",,"  - ""effectiveness of counseling provided during mpox vaccination on the uptake of other recommended vaccines (HPV, HAV, and HBV)""
