"Clinical and Sociodemographic Factors Associated With Ocular Mpox in California, May 2022 to September 2023","Using California STD surveillance data, we found that ocular mpox disproportionately impacts vulnerable communities and that people with ocular mpox less frequently received mpox vaccination.","Wyatt Hanft, Kayla Saadeh, Robert E Snyder, Jessica Watson, Eric C Tang, Eric Chapman, Marisa Ramos, Kelly A Johnson",10.1097/OLQ.0000000000002195,https://doi.org/10.1097/OLQ.0000000000002195,Sexually Transmitted Diseases,1,2025,maybe,"The abstract does not specify the age or pregnancy status of the participants, only referring broadly to 'vulnerable communities' and 'people' within surveillance data. There is no evidence it is limited exclusively to healthy non-pregnant adults.",yes,"The study discusses 'ocular mpox' outcomes and the frequency of 'mpox vaccination', which relates to prevention of mpox complications.",yes,"The study uses surrogate surveillance data to identify associations, suggesting a primary research design such as a cohort or cross-sectional study.",yes,The paper uses human surveillance data from California.,maybe,"The abstract does not explicitly state that it include pregnant women, neonates, children, or adolescents; it only mentions 'people' and 'vulnerable communities'.",maybe,"While the study mentions vaccination status, it does not specify if the timing occurred during pregnancy, childhood, or adolescence.",yes,"The study mentions 'mpox vaccination', which typically refers to vaccinia-based vaccines like JYNNEOS during the 2022-2023 timeframe.",Include,"This study analyzes surveillance data regarding ocular mpox and vaccination status in California. However, it is unclear from the provided text whether the target populations of interest (pregnant women or minors) are included, resulting in 'maybe' decisions for population-specific criteria.",,,3.6,"  - ""Using California STD surveillance data, we found that ocular mpox disproportionately impacts vulnerable communities and that people with ocular mpox less frequently received mpox vaccination.""",,"  - ""Using California STD surveillance data, we found that ocular mpox disproportionately impacts vulnerable communities and that people with ocular mpox less frequently received mpox vaccination.""",,"  - ""Using California STD surveillance data, we found that ocular mpox disproportionately impacts vulnerable communities and that people with ocular mpox less frequently received mpox vaccination.""",,"  - ""Using California STD surveillance data, we found that ocular mpox disproportionately impacts vulnerable communities and that people with ocular mpox less frequently received mpox vaccination.""",,"  - ""Using California STD surveillance data, we found that ocular mpox disproportionately impacts vulnerable communities and that people with ocular mpox less frequently received mpox vaccination.""",,"  - ""Using California STD surveillance data, we found that ocular mpox disproportionately impacts vulnerable communities and that people with ocular mpox less frequently received mpox vaccination.""",,"  - ""Using California STD surveillance data, we found that ocular mpox disproportionately impacts vulnerable communities and that people with ocular mpox less frequently received mpox vaccination.""",
Association Between Maternal Pertussis Vaccination During Pregnancy and Early Childhood Health Outcomes,"Background: Little is known about whether there are any longer-term adverse health effects in children following Tdap (tetanus, diphtheria, and acellular pertussis) vaccination during pregnancy. Objective: To assess the association between maternal Tdap vaccination during pregnancy and risk of the following early childhood adverse health outcomes: (1) infections (upper and lower respiratory tract infections, gastrointestinal infections, and otitis media), (2) pediatric asthma, (3) neoplasm, (4) vision or hearing loss, and (5) urgent and in-patient health services utilization. Methods: This retrospective cohort study used multiple linked health administrative databases in the province of Ontario, Canada containing vaccine information in mothers and information on health outcomes in their children up to age 6 years. Infants exposed to prenatal Tdap were matched 1:5 with unexposed infants and outcomes were compared using hazard ratios and incidence rate ratios. Results: No significant adverse associations between prenatal Tdap and our study outcomes were observed. Inverse associations were found with upper respiratory infections (adjusted incidence rate ratio [aIRR]: 0.96, 95% CI: 0.93-0.99), lower respiratory infections (aIRR: 0.93, 95% CI: 0.89-0.98), gastrointestinal infections (aIRR: 0.88, 95% CI: 0.82-0.94), and urgent and in-patient health service utilization (aIRR: 0.95, 95% CI: 0.94-0.97). Conclusions: Our findings support the long-term safety of Tdap administration in pregnancy.",Meghan Laverty,10.20381/RUOR-24323,https://doi.org/10.20381/RUOR-24323,,0,2020,yes,The study includes pregnant women and children up to 6 years of age.,no,"The study reports on pediatric health safety outcomes (infections, asthma, etc.) but none regarding the prevention of mpox infection, or safety related to mpox/smallpox vaccination.",yes,The study is described as a retrospective cohort study.,yes,This is a human study using health administrative databases for mothers and children.,yes,The study focus is on pregnant women and their children up to age 6.,yes,Participants received the vaccination during pregnancy.,no,"The intervention studied is the Tdap (tetanus, diphtheria, and acellular pertussis) vaccine, not a vaccinia-based mpox or smallpox vaccine.",Exclude,"This study is a retrospective cohort study evaluating children's health outcomes following maternal Tdap vaccination. It fails the inclusion criteria because it assesses the Tdap vaccine rather than vaccinia-based mpox or smallpox vaccines, and it does not report outcomes relevant to mpox prevention or safety.","Relevant Outcomes, Vaccine Type",Vaccine Type,0.1,"  - ""Tdap (tetanus, diphtheria, and acellular pertussis) vaccination during pregnancy.""
