Robust Adaptive Immunity to MPXV in Older People Who Received Childhood Vaccinia Vaccination,"Simple Summary Vaccination against smallpox provides protection from Monkeypox virus, which has recently shown an increase in cases. We assessed adults aged 79–94 years who were vaccinated against smallpox as children and showed both antibody and T-cell memory responses against Monkeypox virus. No such responses were found in unvaccinated individuals. This suggests that receiving the smallpox vaccination as a child can provide long-lasting protection against Monkeypox, decades later.","Chris Davis, J. Zuo, R. Bruton, Marie Hodges, T. Roberts, Maria Manali, Paula Olmo, B. Willett, P. Moss, Helen M. Parry",10.3390/biology15030234,https://doi.org/10.3390/biology15030234,Biology,0,2026,no,"The study is exclusively limited to adults, as participants are aged 79–94 years.",yes,"The study reports effectiveness-related outcomes, specifically antibody and T-cell memory responses.",yes,This is a primary research study evaluating the immune status of a specific cohort.,yes,The study involves human participants aged 79–94.,no,"The participants in the study are adults aged 79–94 rather than children, adolescents, or pregnant women.",yes,The study participants received the vaccine as children.,yes,The study involves historical smallpox (vaccinia) vaccination.,Exclude,"Although the study examines the long-term effects of smallpox vaccination administered during childhood, the actual study participants are adults aged 79–94. Because it does not include children, adolescents, or pregnant women as current participants, it fails the mandatory population criteria.","Population Focus, Target Population",Target Population,0.1,"  - ""assessed adults aged 79–94 years who were vaccinated against smallpox as children""",,"  - ""antibody and T-cell memory responses against Monkeypox virus.""",,"  - ""assessed adults aged 79–94 years who were vaccinated against smallpox as children""",,"  - ""assessed adults aged 79–94 years who were vaccinated against smallpox as children""",,"  - ""assessed adults aged 79–94 years who were vaccinated against smallpox as children""",,"  - ""receiving the smallpox vaccination as a child""",,"  - ""receiving the smallpox vaccination as a child""
