"Very low risk of monkeypox among staff and students after exposure to a confirmed case in educational settings, England, May to July 2022","We investigated a secondary school (11–16 year-olds), a primary school (5–11 year-olds), reception year (4–5 year-olds) and a nursery (2–5 year-olds) following confirmed monkeypox in an adult in each educational setting during June and July 2022. MVA-BN vaccine was offered up to 14 days post exposure to 186 children < 12 years and 21 were vaccinated. No secondary cases occurred among at least 340 exposed students and more than 100 exposed staff during the 28-day follow-up period.","S. Ladhani, F. Aiano, David S. Edwards, S. Perkins, Wazirzada M Khan, Nalini Iyanger, E. Whittaker, Jonathan Cohen, David Ho, S. Hopkins, M. Ramsay, J. Chow",10.2807/1560-7917.ES.2022.27.40.2200734,https://doi.org/10.2807/1560-7917.ES.2022.27.40.2200734,Euro surveillance : bulletin Europeen sur les maladies transmissibles = European communicable disease bulletin,14,2022,yes,"The study includes children and adolescents aged 2 to 16 years, so it is not limited to healthy non-pregnant adults.",yes,The study reports on the prevention of mpox infection (no secondary cases) following post-exposure vaccination.,yes,The study appears to be a case series or observational cohort study investigating exposures and outcomes in educational settings.,yes,The study involves human participants in educational settings (students and staff).,yes,The study includes children and adolescents aged 2 to 16 years.,yes,Participants under 12 years of age received the vaccine post-exposure during childhood.,yes,"The study involves the MVA-BN vaccine, which is a vaccinia-based mpox vaccine.",Include,"This study evaluates the risk of mpox and the effectiveness of the MVA-BN vaccine in a pediatric population ranging from 2 to 16 years old in educational settings. It reports that no secondary cases occurred among exposed students, many of whom were children.",,,5,"  - ""secondary school (11–16 year-olds), a primary school (5–11 year-olds), reception year (4–5 year-olds) and a nursery (2–5 year-olds)""",,"  - ""MVA-BN vaccine was offered up to 14 days post exposure to 186 children < 12 years and 21 were vaccinated.""
