"Mass Smallpox Vaccination and Cardiac Deaths, New York City, 1947","In April 1947, during a smallpox outbreak in New York City (NYC), >6,000,000 people were vaccinated. To determine whether vaccination increased cardiac death, we reviewed NYC death certificates for comparable periods in 1946 and 1948 (N = 81,529) and calculated adjusted relative death rates for the postvaccination period. No increases in cardiac deaths were observed.","L. Thorpe, F. Mostashari, A. Karpati, Steven Schwartz, Susan E. Manning, M. Marx, T. Frieden",10.3201/EID1005.040119,https://doi.org/10.3201/EID1005.040119,Emerging Infectious Diseases,22,2004,yes,"The study involves a mass vaccination of the general population of NYC, exceeding 6,000,000 people, which necessarily includes children, elderly, and other groups beyond healthy non-pregnant adults.",yes,The study reports on cardiac deaths following vaccination.,yes,The study is a primary research investigation reviewing death certificates (observational cohort/ecological study).,yes,The study evaluates human death certificates from a mass vaccination campaign.,maybe,"While the study vaccinated over 6,000,000 people, which would demographically include children, adolescents, and pregnant women in a city-wide campaign, the abstract does not explicitly mention these subgroups or provide stratified analysis for them.",maybe,"As the campaign covered 6,000,000 people in the general population, many participants likely received the vaccine during childhood or adolescence, but this is not explicitly detailed in the provided text.",yes,The study explicitly involves historical smallpox vaccination.,Include,"This study evaluates cardiac deaths following a mass smallpox vaccination campaign in NYC involving over 6,000,000 people. While the broad population size ensures the inclusion of children and adolescents, the abstract lacks explicit confirmation or subgroup analysis for the target pediatric and maternal populations.",,,3.9,"  - ""6,000,000 people were vaccinated.""",,"  - ""reviewed NYC death certificates""
