Mpox Infection in Children—Infection Control Implications for Household Contacts,Abstract Mpox has recently re-emerged as a global entity of concern. We report one of the first pediatric cases in the United States and provide updated recommendations relevant to infection control and prevention measures of those in close contact with mpox.,"Angel N Desai, G. Thompson, Daniel S Dodson, Sonja M Neumeister, Anna M Arutyunova, Katelyn Trigg, D. Blumberg, Stuart H. Cohen",10.1093/ofid/ofad003,https://doi.org/10.1093/ofid/ofad003,Open Forum Infectious Diseases,5,2023,yes,"The study focuses on a pediatric case, meaning it is not limited to healthy adults.",maybe,The abstract mentions recommendations for infection control and prevention measures but does not explicitly state the reporting of primary effectiveness or safety outcomes of a vaccine intervention for the case described.,yes,"The paper reports a case, which constitutes primary research.",yes,The study is a report of a pediatric human case.,yes,"The study describes a pediatric case, which falls under the target population of children/adolescents <18 years.",maybe,The abstract does not specify whether the subject received a vaccine during childhood; it describes an infection case and general prevention recommendations.,maybe,The abstract mentions infection control and prevention measures but does not explicitly mention if the subject received a vaccinia-based or historical smallpox vaccine.,Include,"The paper describes a pediatric mpox case in the United States, meeting target population criteria. However, the abstract is focused on infection control recommendations and it is unclear if any vaccination-specific data (safety or effectiveness) for the patient is recorded.",,,3.6,"  - ""one of the first pediatric cases in the United States""",,"  - ""provide updated recommendations relevant to infection control and prevention measures of those in close contact with mpox.""",,"  - ""one of the first pediatric cases in the United States""",,"  - ""one of the first pediatric cases in the United States""",,"  - ""one of the first pediatric cases in the United States""",,"  - ""one of the first pediatric cases in the United States""
