"Effectiveness of the Modified Vaccinia Ankara Vaccine Against Mpox in Men Who Have Sex With Men: A Retrospective Cohort Analysis, Seattle, Washington","Abstract Background Data on modified Vaccinia Ankara (MVA) vaccine effectiveness against mpox in real-world settings are limited. Methods We performed a retrospective cohort analysis using Cox proportional hazards regression to estimate the association between vaccination and laboratory-confirmed mpox incidence. Study subjects included all men who have sex with men seen in a sexual health clinic in Seattle, Washington, between 1 January 2020 and 31 December 2022. Subjects’ receipt of vaccine and diagnosis with mpox were ascertained from public health vaccine registry and surveillance data. Analyses were adjusted for demographic factors, human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) status, and sexual risk behaviors. Results The incidence of mpox per 100 person-years was 8.83 among patients with 0 doses, 3.32 among patients with 1 dose, and 0.78 among patients with 2 doses of MVA vaccine. Mpox diagnosis was significantly associated with age category 30–39 and 40–51 years, HIV positivity, syphilis diagnosis in the prior year, >10 sex partners in the last year, and having a clinic visit in the last year. In the multivariate model adjusting for these factors, vaccine effectiveness was 81% for 1 dose and 83% for 2 doses. Conclusions These data support the effectiveness of the MVA vaccine—including a single dose of the vaccine—in preventing mpox disease and highlight the appropriateness of risk factor-based prioritization of immunization early in the epidemic. The durability of MVA vaccine-induced immunity is unknown, and at-risk persons should receive 2 doses of MVA.","M. Ramchandani, A. Berzkalns, Chase A. Cannon, Julie Dombrowski, Elizabeth Brown, Eric J. Chow, Elizabeth A. Barash, Sargis Pogosjans, Daniel Smith, Matthew R. Golden",10.1093/ofid/ofad528,https://doi.org/10.1093/ofid/ofad528,Open Forum Infectious Diseases,21,2023,yes,"The study includes individuals who are not healthy, specifically referencing those with 'HIV positivity'.",yes,The study reports on vaccine effectiveness in preventing laboratory-confirmed mpox.,yes,The study is a primary research study using a retrospective cohort analysis.,yes,The study involves human subjects seen at a sexual health clinic.,no,"The study is limited to men who have sex with men and specifically highlights age categories between 30 and 51 years, with no mention of participants under 18, neonates, or pregnant women.",no,"Since the study popluation focuses on adult men, there is no evidence that vaccination occurred during pregnancy, the neonatal period, or childhood.",yes,The study evaluates the Modified Vaccinia Ankara (MVA) vaccine.,Exclude,"While the study evaluates the effectiveness of the MVA vaccine, its population is exclusively adult men who have sex with men. It contains no participants from the required target groups such as children, adolescents, or pregnant women.","Target Population, Vaccination Timing",Target Population,0.1,"  - ""HIV positivity,""",,"  - ""vaccine effectiveness was 81% for 1 dose and 83% for 2 doses.""",,"  - ""retrospective cohort analysis""",,"  - ""Study subjects included all men who have sex with men seen in a sexual health clinic""",,"  - ""Study subjects included all men who have sex with men seen in a sexual health clinic""
