Maternal and Fetal Outcomes Among Pregnant Women With Human Monkeypox Infection in the Democratic Republic of Congo,"Human monkeypox is an endemic disease in rain-forested regions of central Democratic Republic of Congo. We report fetal outcomes for 1 of 4 pregnant women who participated in an observational study at the General Hospital of Kole (Sankuru Province), where 222 symptomatic subjects were followed between 2007 and 2011. Of the 4 pregnant women, 1 gave birth to a healthy infant, 2 had miscarriages in the first trimester, and 1 had fetal death, with the macerated stillborn showing diffuse cutaneous maculopapillary skin lesions involving the head, trunk and extremities, including palms of hands and soles of feet.","P. Mbala, J. Huggins, Therese Riu-Rovira, Steve M Ahuka, Prime M. Mulembakani, A. Rimoin, James W. Martin, J. Muyembe",10.1093/infdis/jix260,https://doi.org/10.1093/infdis/jix260,Journal of Infectious Diseases,290,2017,yes,"The study population consists of pregnant women symptomatic for monkeypox, meaning it is not exclusively limited to healthy non-pregnant adults.",no,"The study reports outcomes following monkeypox infection, such as miscarriage and fetal death. However, it does not report outcomes related to vaccination safety or the effectiveness of the vaccine in preventing infection or death.",yes,The study is an observational primary research project following symptomatic subjects.,yes,"The study participants are pregnant women, which are human subjects.",yes,The study specifically includes 4 pregnant women.,no,There is no mention of the participants receiving any vaccine during pregnancy or otherwise; the study focus is on natural infection outcomes.,no,The study describes the progression and outcomes of human monkeypox infection but does not involve or mention vaccinia-based mpox vaccines or historical smallpox vaccines.,Exclude,"This study focuses exclusively on the maternal and fetal outcomes of monkeypox infection during pregnancy in the Democratic Republic of Congo. It does not involve any vaccination intervention, thus failing multiple mandatory criteria related to vaccine type, timing, and related outcomes.","Relevant Outcomes, Vaccination Timing, Vaccine Type",Vaccine Type,0.1,"  - ""Of the 4 pregnant women, 1 gave birth to a healthy infant, 2 had miscarriages in the first trimester, and 1 had fetal death,""
