  - ""Fifteen publications were included""",,"  - ""systematic review and meta-analysis of randomized-controlled trials (RCTs)""",,"  - ""evaluate the safety and immunogenicity of the Modified Vaccinia Ankara (MVA) vaccine.""",
"Smallpox vaccine adverse events among civilians--United States, February 18-24, 2003.","During the civilian smallpox vaccination program, CDC and state health departments are conducting surveillance for vaccine-associated adverse events. In the first stage of the program, active surveillance is being conducted for potentially life-threatening, moderate-to-severe, and other serious adverse events and for vaccinia transmission to contacts of vaccinees (Table). Nonserious events are reported through passive surveillance and are expected to be underreported. This report summarizes smallpox vaccine adverse events reported among civilians vaccinated as of February 21, 2003, and received by CDC from the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS) as of February 24.",,10.1001/jama.289.13.1627,https://doi.org/10.1001/jama.289.13.1627,MMWR. Morbidity and mortality weekly report,2,2003,maybe,"The paper focuses on the 'civilian' population in the US. It does not explicitly state that the population was exclusively healthy non-pregnant adults, but it doesn't characterize the group further beyond 'civilians'.",yes,"The study reports on adverse events, both serious and nonserious.",yes,The study is a surveillance report (a type of primary observational research/cohort series).,yes,The study reports on adverse events in human civilians.,maybe,"The abstract does not specify whether pregnant women, neonates, children, or adolescents were included in the 'civilian' surveillance population. In 2003, the US civilian smallpox vaccination program was primarily targeted at healthcare workers and first responders (adults), and pregnancy was generally a contraindication.",maybe,"It is unclear if any of the civilians were vaccinated during pregnancy, childhood, or adolescence, as the specific ages and pregnancy statuses of the civilians are not detailed in the abstract.",yes,The study explicitly involves the smallpox vaccine.,Include,"This report summarizes surveillance data for adverse e