[Research progress on the effectiveness of smallpox vaccination against mpox virus infection].,"With the expansion of mpox virus infection from endemic to a global epidemic in 2022, the WHO declared that the mpox event constituted a Public Health Emergency of International Concern. Due to the high degree of gene sequence similarity among orthopox viruses and cross-reactive antibodies induced by orthoviruses, smallpox vaccination may affect the immune response induced by mpox virus infection. The analysis of the protective effects of smallpox vaccination against mpox virus infection will help define the focus of prevention and control. In this review, we clarify the protection of the smallpox vaccine against mpox virus infection by analyzing the correlation between smallpox vaccination, immune response status, and clinical data and providing evidence for the prevention, control, and strategies of mpox epidemics.","Y. Xu, M. Jiang, Y. L. Cao, Y. Sun, Q. R. Huang, W. Z. Yang, L. Z. Feng",10.3760/cma.j.cn112338-20221102-00934,https://doi.org/10.3760/cma.j.cn112338-20221102-00934,Zhonghua liu xing bing xue za zhi = Zhonghua liuxingbingxue zazhi,1,2023,maybe,The abstract describes general clinical data and immune status but does not specify whether the population is limited to or includes specific groups.,yes,The study explicitly aims to clarify the protection and protective effects of the smallpox vaccine against mpox infection.,maybe,"The paper describes itself as a review, though it is not explicitly labeled as a systematic review or meta-analysis.",yes,"The analysis uses clinical data, which implies the study of human subjects.",no,"There is no mention of pregnant women, neonates, children, or adolescents in the provided abstract.",no,"The abstract does not specify whether vaccination occurred during pregnancy, childhood, or adolescence.",yes,The study involves the historical smallpox vaccine and its cross-reactive protection against mpox.,Exclude,"This paper is a general review of smallpox vaccine effectiveness against mpox virus infection based on clinical data, but it provides no evidence of including or focusing on the required target populations such as children or pregnant women.","Target Population, Vaccination Timing",Target Population,0.1,"  - ""analyzing the correlation between smallpox vaccination, immune response status, and clinical data""",,"  - ""In this review, we clarify the protection of the smallpox vaccine against mpox virus infection""",,"  - ""In this review, we clarify the protection of the smallpox vaccine against mpox virus infection""",,"  - ""analyzing the correlation between smallpox vaccination, immune response status, and clinical data""",,"  - ""In this review, we clarify the protection of the smallpox vaccine against mpox virus infection""
