"Fatal Cowpox Virus Infection in Human Fetus, France, 2017","Cowpox virus (CPXV) has an animal reservoir and is typically transmitted to humans by contact with infected animals. In 2017, CPXV infection of a pregnant woman in France led to the death of her fetus. Fetal death after maternal orthopoxvirus (smallpox) vaccination has been reported; however, this patient had not been vaccinated. Investigation of the patient’s domestic animals failed to demonstrate prevalence of CPXV infection among them. The patient’s diagnosis was confirmed by identifying CPXV DNA in all fetal and maternal biopsy samples and infectious CPXV in biopsy but not plasma samples. This case of fetal death highlights the risk for complications of orthopoxvirus infection during pregnancy. Among orthopoxviruses, fetal infection has been reported for variola virus and vaccinia virus; our findings suggest that CPXV poses the same threats for infection complications as vaccinia virus.","Audrey Ferrier, Gaelle Frénois-Veyrat, E. Schvoerer, S. Hénard, Fanny Jarjaval, I. Drouet, Hawa Timera, L. Boutin, Estelle Mosca, C. Peyrefitte, O. Ferraris",10.3201/eid2710.204818,https://doi.org/10.3201/eid2710.204818,Emerging Infectious Diseases,27,2021,yes,The study focuses on a pregnant woman and a fetus.,yes,"The study reports on fetal death, which is a significant complication/safety outcome.",yes,This is a case report describing a single medical instance.,yes,This is a report focusing on human subjects (a pregnant woman and fetus).,yes,The study specifically involves a pregnant woman and a fetus.,no,The participant did not receive a vaccine; the study explicitly states she was not vaccinated.,no,The study does not evaluate a vaccine; it investigates a natural Cowpox virus (CPXV) infection in an unvaccinated patient.,Exclude,"This case report describes a fatal cowpox virus infection in a fetus, but the mother was explicitly stated to be unvaccinated. Because the study investigates a natural viral infection rather than the effects of a vaccinia-based or smallpox vaccine, it does not meet the specified vaccine-related criteria.","Vaccination Timing, Vaccine Type",Vaccine Type,0.1,"  - ""In 2017, CPXV infection of a pregnant woman in France led to the death of her fetus.""",,"  - ""In 2017, CPXV infection of a pregnant woman in France led to the death of her fetus.""",,"  - ""In 2017, CPXV infection of a pregnant woman in France led to the death of her fetus.""
