"Smallpox vaccine adverse events among civilians--United States, March 4-10, 2003.","During the civilian smallpox vaccination program, CDC, the Food and Drug Administration, and state health departments are conducting surveillance for vaccine-associated adverse events. In the first stage of the program, active surveillance is being conducted for potentially life-threatening, moderate-to-severe, and other serious adverse events and for vaccinia transmission to contacts of vaccinees (Table). Nonserious events are reported through passive surveillance and are expected to be underreported. This report summarizes smallpox vaccine adverse events reported among civilians vaccinated as of March 7, 2003, and among contacts of vaccinees, received by CDC from the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS) as of March 10.",,10.1001/jama.289.15.1921,https://doi.org/10.1001/jama.289.15.1921,MMWR. Morbidity and mortality weekly report,5,2003,no,The 2003 civilian smallpox vaccination program was primarily for adult healthcare workers and public health response teams; the study does not indicate it included any participants besides these groups.,yes,The study specifically monitors and reports on vaccine-associated adverse events.,yes,This is a primary research surveillance report on civilian smallpox vaccination adverse events.,yes,The study involves human civilians vaccinated in a national program.,no,"The study does not mention the inclusion of pregnant women, neonates, children, or adolescents as vaccine recipients in the reported program period.",no,"Because the study lacks evidence of including children or pregnant women in the vaccination program, participants did not receive researchers during these life stages.",yes,The study evaluates smallpox vaccine adverse events.,Exclude,"The paper describes a surveillance program for adverse events from smallpox vaccination; however, the participants are civilians from the 2003 program which targeted adult healthcare workers, and there is no evidence of inclusion of children, adolescents, or pregnant women. Because it fails to meet the target population criteria, it is excluded.","Population Focus, Target Population, Vaccination Timing",Target Population,0.1,"  - ""summarizes smallpox vaccine adverse events reported among civilians vaccinated as of March 7, 2003,""
