Adverse events occurring after smallpox vaccination.,"We reviewed the literature on adverse events reported to occur after smallpox vaccination. Nearly one-half of the United States population is vaccinia-naïve and may be at risk for development of serious adverse events. We describe the clinical features of postvaccinial central nervous system disease, progressive vaccinia, eczema vaccinatum, accidental implantations, ""generalized vaccinia,"" and the common erythematous and/or urticarial rashes. In the 1960s, death occurred approximately once in every million primary vaccinations, with fatalities resulting from progressive vaccinia, postvaccinial encephalitis, and eczema vaccinatum. Death in revaccinees occurred less commonly and almost entirely from progressive vaccinia. In today's population, death rates might be higher because of the increased prevalence of immune deficiency and atopic dermatitis.","Joseph M. Lane, J. Goldstein",10.1016/S1045-1870(03)00032-3,https://doi.org/10.1016/S1045-1870(03)00032-3,Seminars in Pediatric Infectious Diseases,52,2003,yes,"The study includes participants with conditions such as immune deficiency and atopic dermatitis, and so is not limited to exclusively healthy subjects.",yes,The study reports on serious adverse events and fatalities.,yes,"The study is an evidence synthesis, specifically a literature review.",yes,The study reviews clinical features and fatality rates in the United States population.,maybe,"The abstract references 'primary vaccinations' in the 1960s and is published in a pediatric journal, but it does not specify the age of the participants in the text provided.",maybe,"While historical 'primary vaccinations' often occurred in childhood, the abstract does not explicitly state that the participants were vaccinated during the pediatric period.",yes,The study focuses on the 'smallpox vaccination' and 'vaccinia'.,Include,"This paper is a literature review of adverse events and deaths following vaccinia-based smallpox vaccination. Although the publication venue and focus on historical primary vaccinations suggest inclusion of pediatric populations, the abstract text does not explicitly confirm participant ages, resulting in uncertainty for the target population criteria.",,,4.2,"  - ""In today's population, death rates might be higher because of the increased prevalence of immune deficiency and atopic dermatitis.""",,"  - ""We reviewed the literature on adverse events reported to occur after smallpox vaccination.""
