Breakthrough infection and reinfection in patients with mpox,"Recently, patients with Mpox breakthrough infection or reinfection were constantly reported. However, the induction, risk factors, and important clinical symptoms of breakthrough infection and reinfection of Mpox virus (MPXV), as well as the factors affecting the effectiveness of Mpox vaccine are not characterized. Herein, a literature review was preformed to summarize the risk factors and important clinical symptoms of patients with Mpox breakthrough infection or reinfection, as well as the factors affecting the effectiveness of smallpox vaccine against Mpox. Results showed that MSM sexual behavior, condomless sexual behavior, multiple sexual partners, close contact, HIV infection, and the presence of comorbidity are important risk factors for Mpox breakthrough infection and reinfection. Genital ulcers, proctitis, and lymphadenopathy are the important clinical symptoms of Mpox breakthrough infection and reinfection. The effectiveness of emergent vaccination of smallpox vaccine for post‐exposure of MPXV is associated with smallpox vaccination history, interval between exposure and vaccination, and history of HIV infection. This review provides a better understanding for the risk factors and important clinical symptoms of Mpox breakthrough infection and reinfection, as well as the formulation of Mpox vaccine vaccination strategies.","Wenyi Jiang, Yibo Hu, Xiu Yang, Lingli Hou, Jingjing Zhang, Hong Niu, Congxia Hu, Jihui Lin",10.1002/rmv.2522,https://doi.org/10.1002/rmv.2522,Reviews in Medical Virology,8,2024,maybe,"The study focuses on risk groups such as MSM and HIV-infected individuals. It does not explicitly exclude or include specific age groups or pregnancy statuses, though the demographic described (MSM, sexual behavior) strongly suggests it is not limited to healthy non-pregnant adults.",yes,The paper reports on vaccine effectiveness and clinical symptoms (breakthrough infection).,yes,"The paper is a literature review, which is considered an evidence synthesis study.",yes,"The study reviews human clinical data, including symptoms and sexual behaviors.",no,"The abstract does not mention pregnant women, neonates, children, or adolescents. It focuses on MSM and individuals with HIV/comorbidities.",no,"The abstract discusses breakthrough infections and post-exposure vaccination but does not specify that vaccination occurred during pregnancy, the neonatal period, childhood, or adolescence.",yes,The study specifically evaluates the effectiveness of the smallpox vaccine against Mpox.,Exclude,"This literature review explores breakthrough infections and smallpox vaccine effectiveness against mpox, specifically identifying risk factors like MSM sexual behavior and HIV infection. However, it does not include the target populations of pregnant women, neonates, or children required for this review.","Target Population, Vaccination Timing",Target Population,0.1,"  - ""MSM sexual behavior, condomless sexual behavior, multiple sexual partners, close contact, HIV infection, and the presence of comorbidity are important risk factors""",,"  - ""a literature review was preformed to summarize the risk factors and important clinical symptoms of patients with Mpox breakthrough infection or reinfection, as well as the factors affecting the effectiveness of smallpox vaccine against Mpox.""
