Mpox Neutralizing Antibody Response to LC16m8 Vaccine in Healthy Adults.,"Mpox Neutralizing Antibody Response to LC16m8 VaccineIn this study of 50 healthy volunteers in Japan, a smallpox vaccine (LC16m8) exhibited a robust neutralizing antibody response against two strains of the mpox virus. With a 94% ""take"" rate by day 14, seroconversion rates on day 28 were 72 and 70% against the Zr599 and Liberia strains, respectively, decreasing to 30% for both on day 168; no serious adverse events occurred.","E. Morino, S. Mine, N. Tomita, Yukari Uemura, Yosuke Shimizu, S. Saito, Tetsuya Suzuki, N. Okumura, H. Iwasaki, Junko Terada, A. Ainai, Yusuke Sakai, Eunsil Park, Sayuri Seki, D. Akazawa, Masayuki Shimojima, N. Shiwa-Sudo, Milagros Virhuez-Mendoza, Kosuke Miyauchi, Saya Moriyama, N. Iwata-Yoshikawa, Michiko Harada, Shigeyoshi Harada, Takayuki Hishiki, R. Kotaki, T. Matsumura, Sho Miyamoto, T. Kanno, Masanori Isogawa, Koichi Watashi, N. Nagata, Hideki Ebihara, Yoshimasa Takahashi, Ken Maeda, T. Matano, T. Wakita, Tadaki Suzuki, W. Sugiura, N. Ohmagari, M. Ujiie",10.1056/EVIDoa2300290,https://doi.org/10.1056/EVIDoa2300290,NEJM Evidence,15,2024,no,The study title and content explicitly state the participants were healthy adults. Inclusion criteria requires the study NOT be exclusively limited to healthy non-pregnant adults.,yes,The study reports on safety (no serious adverse events) and immunogenicity outcomes (neutralizing antibody response).,yes,This is a primary research study involving 50 volunteers.,yes,"The study was conducted in 50 healthy volunteers, which are humans.",no,"The study was conducted exclusively in healthy adults, and does not mention pregnant women, neonates, or children.",no,"Participants were healthy adults, not vaccinated during pregnancy, the neonatal period, or childhood.",yes,The study used the LC16m8 smallpox vaccine.,Exclude,"This study is excluded because it focused exclusively on healthy human adults and did not include the target populations of pregnant women, neonates, or children. Although it evaluated a relevant vaccine (LC16m8) and reported safety outcomes, it failed the population-based inclusion criteria.","Population Focus, Target Population, Vaccination Timing",Population Focus,0.1,"  - ""In this study of 50 healthy volunteers in Japan,""",,"  - ""a smallpox vaccine (LC16m8) exhibited a robust neutralizing antibody response""
