en.2022.48987,https://doi.org/10.1001/jamanetworkopen.2022.48987,JAMA Network Open,13,2023,yes,"The study focuses on patients aged 5 years or older with a history of MIS-C, which is not limited to healthy non-pregnant adults.",yes,The study reports adverse reactions (safety outcomes) following vaccination.,yes,"The study is a cross-sectional study, which is a primary research design.",yes,The study involves human patients (children and adolescents).,yes,"The study includes patients with a history of MIS-C, typically children and adolescents (specifically mentioned as starting at age 5).",yes,The study investigates vaccination in children/adolescents (age 5+).,no,"The study specifically investigates COVID-19 vaccination, not vaccinia-based or smallpox vaccines.",Exclude,This study is a cross-sectional examination of children and adolescents vaccinated against COVID-19 after a history of MIS-C. It fails the inclusion criteria because it focuses on COVID-19 vaccines rather than the required vaccinia-based or historical smallpox vaccines.,Vaccine Type,Vaccine Type,0.1,"  - ""This cross-sectional study examines adverse reactions after COVID-19 vaccination among patients aged 5 years or older who have a history of multisystem inflammatory syndrome in children.""",,"  - ""This cross-sectional study examines adverse reactions after COVID-19 vaccination among patients aged 5 years or older who have a history of multisystem inflammatory syndrome in children.""",,"  - ""This cross-sectional study examines adverse reactions after COVID-19 vaccination among patients aged 5 years or older who have a history of multisystem inflammatory syndrome in children.""",,"  - ""This cross-sectional study examines adverse reactions after COVID-19 vaccination among patients aged 5 years or older who have a history of multisystem inflammatory syndrome in children.""",,"  - ""This cross-sectional study examines adverse reactions after COVID-19 vaccination among patients aged 5 years or older wh