[Vaccinia autoinoculata during pregnancy].,"A 21 year old woman received a smallpox revaccination during the fifth to sixth month of pregnancy. She developed accidental vaccinia by autoinoculation and, five weeks later, gave birth to a healthy child.",N. Walter,,,"Der Hautarzt; Zeitschrift fur Dermatologie, Venerologie, und verwandte Gebiete",1,1979,yes,"The study concerns a pregnant individual, thus it is not limited to healthy non-pregnant adults.",yes,The study reports complications (accidental vaccinia by autoinoculation) and the health status of the infant.,yes,This is a case report of a single patient.,yes,The study describes a clinical case in a human patient.,yes,The participant was in her fifth to sixth month of pregnancy.,yes,The patient received the vaccine during pregnancy.,yes,The study involves a smallpox revaccination.,Include,"This case report describes a 21-year-old woman who received a smallpox revaccination during her second trimester of pregnancy. The study details the subsequent development of accidental vaccinia and the birth of a healthy child, meeting all inclusion criteria for a study on smallpox/mpox vaccination during pregnancy.",,,5,"  - ""A 21 year old woman received a smallpox revaccination during the fifth to sixth month of pregnancy.""",,"  - ""She developed accidental vaccinia by autoinoculation and, five weeks later, gave birth to a healthy child.""",,"  - ""A 21 year old woman received a smallpox revaccination during the fifth to sixth month of pregnancy.""
