Practical Aspects of Epidemiology and Vaccine Prevention,"Relevance. After vaccination against smallpox is completed, more than 50% of the population are not immune to pathogens of the genus Orthopoxvirus, which creates the risk of mass infection if the smallpox virus is used as a biological weapon. Aim. To assess the correlations between humoral immunity, clinical signs during a vaccination period and, sex and age characteristics of vaccinia virus https://doi.org/10.31631/2073-3046-2020-19-1-77-82 * Для переписки: Белявская Валентина Александровна, д. б. н., профессор, ведущий научный сотрудник ФБУН ГНЦ ВБ «Вектор», 630559, Новосибирская обл., п. Кольцово. +7 (383) 336-47-00, belyavskaya_va@vector.nsc.ru. ©Ермилова О. С. и др. ** For correspondence: Belyavskaya Valentina A., Dr. Sci. (Biol.), professor, leading researcher of State Scientific Centre of Virology and Biotechnology «Vector» of Rospotrebnadzor., Koltsovo, 630559 Russian Federation. +7 (383) 336-47-00, belyavskaya_va@vector.nsc.ru. ©Ermilova OS et al. Э п и де м и ол ог и я и В а кц и н оп р оф и ла кт и ка . Т ом 1 9 , No 1 /E p id em io lo gy a n d V a cc in a l P re ve n ti on . V ol . 1 9 , N o 1 78 Практические аспекты эпидемиологии и вакцинопрофилактики Practical Aspects of Epidemiology and Vaccine Prevention","О. С. Ермилова, З. И. Гинько, В. А. Белявская, Новосибирской обл",,,,0,2020,maybe,The abstract mentions age characteristics but does not specify if the study avoids being exclusively limited to healthy non-pregnant adults. There is no mention of pregnant women or children in the provided text.,yes,The study evaluates humoral immunity and clinical signs during the vaccination period. Clinical signs often include common adverse reactions to smallpox/vaccinia vaccination.,yes,The study aim suggests a primary research study assessing correlations in a vaccinated population.,yes,The assessment of sex and age characteristics and clinical signs suggests a human study.,maybe,"The text does not state