"Effectiveness of one dose of MVA-BN vaccine against mpox infection in males in Ontario, Canada: A target trial emulation","Background: Limited evidence is available on the real-world effectiveness of modified vaccinia Ankara-Bavarian Nordic vaccine (MVA-BN) against mpox infection. Methods: We emulated a target trial using linked databases in Ontario, Canada to estimate the effectiveness of one dose of MVA-BN. Our study included males aged [≤]18 years who: (1) had a history of syphilis testing and a laboratory-confirmed bacterial sexually transmitted infection (STI) in the prior year; or (2) filled a prescription for HIV pre-exposure prophylaxis in the prior year. On each day between June 12, 2022 and October 27, 2022, males who had been vaccinated 15 days prior were matched 1:1 with unvaccinated males by age, geographic region, prior HIV diagnosis, number of bacterial STI diagnoses in the previous three years, and receipt of any non-MVA-BN vaccine in the previous year. We used a Cox proportional hazards model to estimate the hazard ratio comparing the incidence of mpox between the two groups, and calculated vaccine effectiveness as (1-HR)x100. Results: Each group included 3,204 males. A total of 71 mpox infections were diagnosed over the study period, with 0.09 (95% confidence interval [CI], 0.05-0.13) per 1000 person-days for the vaccinated group and 0.20 (95%CI, 0.15-0.27) per 1000 person-days for the unvaccinated group. Estimated vaccine effectiveness of one dose of MVA-BN against mpox infection was 59% (95%CI, 31-76%). Conclusions: This study, conducted in the context of a targeted vaccination program and evolving outbreak, suggests that one dose of MVA-BN is moderately effective in preventing mpox infection.","Christine Navarro MD MSc, Cindy Lau Mph, S. Buchan, Ann N. Burchell, S. Nasreen, Lindsay Friedman Mph, E. O. Mph, Peter C Austin, D. H. Tan, J. G. M. MSc, Jeffrey C. Kwong, Sharmistha Mishra, Victoria Street, Lievre Ka, Shing",10.1101/2023.10.04.23296566,https://doi.org/10.1101/2023.10.04.23296566,medRxiv,9,2023,no,"The study population consists of adult males with HIV PrEP use or STI histories. While the text contains the symbol '[≤]18', the inclusion criteria of STI testing and HIV PrEP usage in the context of the 2022 Ontario mpox outbreak indicate a focus on the adult (≥18 years) male population, thus making it exclusively limited to non-pregnant adults.",yes,The study reports vaccine effectiveness against mpox infection.,yes,The study is a target trial emulation (a primary cohort study).,yes,The study is a human database study involving matched groups of vaccinated and unvaccinated males.,no,"The study focuses on adult males and does not include pregnant women, neonates, or children. Although the text renders the age as '[≤]18', the medical history criteria (PrEP and syphilis history) and the epidemiological context of the study in Ontario indicate it targeted adults ≥18 years.",no,"Based on the participant risk factors and the timing of the 2022 mpox vaccination program, participants were vaccinated during adulthood rather than during pregnancy, the neonatal period, or childhood.",yes,The study evaluates the MVA-BN vaccine.,Exclude,"This target trial emulation study evaluates the effectiveness of the MVA-BN vaccine in adult males in Ontario. However, it does not include pregnant women, children, or adolescents, which are the required target populations for this review.","Population Focus, Target Population, Vaccination Timing",Target Population,0.1,"  - ""Our study included males aged [≤]18 years who: (1) had a history of syphilis testing and a laboratory-confirmed bacterial sexually transmitted infection (STI) in the prior year; or (2) filled a prescription for HIV pre-exposure prophylaxis in the prior year.""",,"  - ""Estimated vaccine effectiveness of one dose of MVA-BN against mpox infection was 59% (95%CI, 31-76%).""",,"  - ""We emulated a target trial using linked databases in Ontario, Canada to estimate the effectiveness of one dose of MVA-BN.""",,"  - ""Our study included males aged [≤]18 years who: (1) had a history of syphilis testing and a laboratory-confirmed bacterial sexually transmitted infection (STI) in the prior year; or (2) filled a prescription for HIV pre-exposure prophylaxis in the prior year.""",,"  - ""Our study included males aged [≤]18 years who: (1) had a history of syphilis testing and a laboratory-confirmed bacterial sexually transmitted infection (STI) in the prior year; or (2) filled a prescription for HIV pre-exposure prophylaxis in the prior year.""",,"  - ""Our study included males aged [≤]18 years who: (1) had a history of syphilis testing and a laboratory-confirmed bacterial sexually transmitted infection (STI) in the prior year; or (2) filled a prescription for HIV pre-exposure prophylaxis in the prior year.""",,"  - ""Our study included males aged [≤]18 years who: (1) had a history of syphilis testing and a laboratory-confirmed bacterial sexually transmitted infection (STI) in the prior year; or (2) filled a prescription for HIV pre-exposure prophylaxis in the prior year.""
