"Safety, Immunogenicity, and Efficacy of the NVX-CoV2373 COVID-19 Vaccine in Adolescents","Key Points Question Is NVX-CoV2373 safe, immunogenic, and effective in adolescents aged 12 to 17 years? Findings In this phase 3 randomized clinical trial including 2247 adolescents, neutralizing antibody responses were noninferior compared with those of young adults aged 18 to 25 years (effectiveness). Vaccine efficacy was 79.5%, and reactogenicity was mostly mild to moderate and transient; no safety concerns were identified. Meaning These findings indicate that NVX-CoV2373 was safe, immunogenic, and efficacious in preventing COVID-19 in adolescents.","G. Áñez, L. Dunkle, C. Gay, K. Kotloff, J. Adelglass, B. Essink, J. Campbell, S. Cloney-Clark, Mingzhu Zhu, J. Plested, Pavitra Roychoudhury, A. Greninger, N. Patel, Alice McGarry, W. Woo, I. Cho, G. Glenn, F. Dubovsky",10.1001/jamanetworkopen.2023.9135,https://doi.org/10.1001/jamanetworkopen.2023.9135,JAMA Network Open,38,2023,yes,The study population consists of adolescents aged 12 to 17 years.,yes,The study reports safety (reactogenicity) and effectiveness (vaccine efficacy) outcomes.,yes,The study is a phase 3 randomized clinical trial.,yes,The study is a clinical trial involving human participants.,yes,The study specifically includes adolescents aged 12 to 17 years.,yes,The vaccine was administered to participants during their adolescence.,no,"The study investigates the NVX-CoV2373 COVID-19 vaccine, which is not a vaccinia-based mpox or smallpox vaccine.",Exclude,"This phase 3 randomized clinical trial evaluates the NVX-CoV2373 vaccine in adolescents. While it meets population and outcome criteria, it is excluded because it investigates a COVID-19 vaccine rather than a vaccinia-based mpox or smallpox vaccine.",Vaccine Type,Vaccine Type,0.1,"  - ""Is NVX-CoV2373 safe, immunogenic, and effective in adolescents aged 12 to 17 years?""",,"  - ""Vaccine efficacy was 79.5%, and reactogenicity was mostly mild to moderate""",,"  - 