The Durability and Avidity of MPXV-specific Antibodies Induced by the Two-dose MVA-BN Mpox Vaccine,"The 2022 global outbreak of clade IIb mpox was the first major outbreak of mpox outside of African nations. To control the outbreak, vaccination campaigns were begun using the third-generation orthopoxvirus vaccine MVA-BN. During the vaccination campaign, we launched the New York City Observational Study of Mpox Immunity (NYC OSMI). NYC OSMI is a longitudinal study that enrolled 171 MVA-BN vaccinees with or without prior smallpox vaccination and mpox convalescent individuals. Study participants had blood drawn prior to vaccination, after one dose, and after two doses. Mpox virus (MPXV) neutralizing titers in sera reach a comparable peak in naive and experienced vaccinees. However, neutralizing titers return to baseline in less than one year for naive individuals, while remaining elevated in those with prior smallpox vaccination. Both naive and experienced individuals generate robust, immunodominant IgG responses against MPXV H3 and A35, but with significantly lower avidity in naive vaccinees. Their vaccinia virus homologs H3 and A33 have previously been shown to be protective targets for orthopoxvirus infection and disease in mouse models. These data highlight a low avidity antibody response elicited by MVA-BN that is short-lived in naive vaccinees. This study supports the need for studies of long-term protection from MVA-BN, the potential need for booster doses, and further development of next-generation orthopoxvirus vaccines.","A. Oom, A. Kottkamp, K. K. Wilson, M. Yonatan, S. Rettig, H. Youn, M. Tuen, Y. Shah, A. L. DuMont, M. Samanovic, R. Duerr, M. Mulligan, Nyc Osmi Study Group",10.1101/2024.01.28.24301893,https://doi.org/10.1101/2024.01.28.24301893,medRxiv,3,2024,no,"The study cohort consists of 171 vaccinees and convalescent individuals, likely adults given the inclusion of those with prior smallpox vaccination (routine vaccination stopped decades ago), and there is no mention of pregnant women or other specific demographics beyond mpox history.",no,"The study reports immunogenicity (IgG responses and neutralizing titers) but does not report clinical effectiveness outcomes such as prevention of infection, hospitalization, or death.",yes,"The study is described as a longitudinal study, which is a type of primary cohort research.",yes,The study enrolled 171 human participants for blood draws and analysis.,no,"There is no mention of pregnant women, neonates, children, or adolescents in the study population.",no,"The vaccination occurred during the 2022 global outbreak, but there is no indication that participants received the vaccine during pregnancy, the neonatal period, or childhood.",yes,The study evaluates the MVA-BN vaccine and includes individuals with prior smallpox vaccination.,Exclude,This longitudinal study focuses on antibody durability in a general cohort of 171 vaccinees. It fails multiple mandatory criteria as it does not include the target populations of pregnant women or children and does not report clinical outcomes like prevention of infection.,"Population Focus, Relevant Outcomes, Target Population, Vaccination Timing",Target Population,0.1,"  - ""NYC OSMI is a longitudinal study that enrolled 171 MVA-BN vaccinees with or without prior smallpox vaccination and mpox convalescent individuals.""",,"  - ""naive and experienced individuals generate robust, immunodominant IgG responses against MPXV H3 and A35,""
