"Smallpox vaccine adverse events among civilians--United States, January 24-February 18, 2003.","During the civilian smallpox vaccination program, CDC and state health departments are conducting surveillance for vaccine-associated adverse events. In the first stage of the program, active surveillance is being conducted for potentially life-threatening, moderate-to-severe, and other serious adverse events and for vaccinia transmission to contacts of vaccinees (Table). Nonserious events are reported via passive surveillance and are expected to be underreported. This report summarizes smallpox vaccine adverse events reported among civilians vaccinated as of February 14, 2003, and received by CDC from the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS) as of February 18.",,10.1037/e307112005-004,https://doi.org/10.1037/e307112005-004,MMWR. Morbidity and mortality weekly report,9,2003,maybe,The study reports on adverse events among 'civilians' in a general vaccination program; it does not specify whether the population is exclusively limited to healthy non-pregnant adults.,yes,The study specifically reports on safety outcomes including vaccine-associated adverse events.,yes,"The report is a surveillance summary, which functions as a primary research study/cohort study style analysis of vaccine recipients.",yes,The study involves human civilians receiving vaccines.,maybe,"The abstract mentions 'civilians' generally and does not explicitly state the inclusion of pregnant women, neonates, children, or adolescents. In 2003, the civilian smallpox program was primarily targeted at healthcare workers and first responders (adults).",maybe,"There is no explicit information stating that participants received the vaccine during pregnancy, childhood, or adolescence, as the target population for this program was typically adult first responders.",yes,"The study involves the 'smallpox vaccine' used in the 2003 US program, which was the vaccinia-based Dryvax vaccine.",Include,"This report details adverse events from the 2003 US civilian smallpox vaccination program. While it covers relevant vaccine types and safety outcomes, it is unclear if the participants include the specific target priority populations such as children or pregnant women.",,,3.4,"  - ""This report summarizes smallpox vaccine adverse events reported among civilians vaccinated as of February 14, 2003,""",,"  - ""This report summarizes smallpox vaccine adverse events reported among civilians vaccinated as of February 14, 2003,""
