Monkeypox virus vaccine evolution and global preparedness for vaccination,"The recent emergence of monkeypox (MPX) has created a global threat. The number of infected and suspected cases of MPX is increasing in different parts of the world, especially in non-African countries. However, vaccines are available to fight against this disease. It has been observed that smallpox vaccines can be used to protect against MPX. The present article highlights the significant points and various issues for vaccines and vaccinations that should be considered related to MPX. This paper illustrates current vaccines for smallpox that can be utilized to protect against MPX infection. The article also describes the different significant research on MPXV, especially smallpox vaccines, and its outcome in MPX infection. We have also tried to depict the smallpox vaccination eradication model through the statistical interface using smallpox eradication data from Central and West Africa between 1967 and 1972. We suggest that these models might be helpful for the eradication of MPX in the middle to low-economic countries. Simultaneously, we have also discussed vaccination preparedness in different countries like the USA, UK, Canada, Denmark, Germany, etc. Our report might be helpful to scientists and policymakers in understanding the vaccines and vaccination against MPX and formulating effective strategies to fight against the disease.","C. Chakraborty, M. Bhattacharya, Ashish Ranjan Sharma, K. Dhama",10.1016/j.intimp.2022.109346,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.intimp.2022.109346,International Immunopharmacology,26,2022,maybe,The paper is a general review and does not specify a specific study population or limit itself to healthy adults.,yes,The article discusses vaccine outcomes in mpox infection from existing research.,no,"The study is a narrative report or perspective piece that summarizes research and depicts a statistical model, which does not qualify as primary research (RCT, cohort, etc.) or a systematic review.",yes,The article discusses vaccines and vaccination strategies for humans.,no,"The text does not mention the inclusion of pregnant women, neonates, children, or adolescents.",no,The study does not involve or report on vaccination timing for the specific target subpopulations.,yes,The study explicitly discusses smallpox vaccines (vaccinia-based) for mpox prevention.,Exclude,"This paper is a narrative review and statistical modeling report rather than a primary research study or systematic review. Furthermore, it does not specifically include or address the target populations of pregnant women, neonates, or children.","Study Design, Target Population, Vaccination Timing",Target Population,0.1,"  - ""The present article highlights the significant points and various issues for vaccines and vaccinations that should be considered related to MPX.""
