Clinical characteristics of monkeypox vaccine injection site reactions: A cohort of seven patients,"Monkeypox (Mpox) infections are considered a public health emergency, prompting the need for the administration of a preventative vaccine to high‐risk individuals.To describe the clinical course of dermatologic reactions to Mpox vaccine over time.Seven recipients of the Mpox vaccine, administered via intradermal injection, were observed over time, and the dermatologic reactions to this vaccine were recorded.All seven recipients experienced mild to moderate localized reactions to Mpox vaccine to either the primary or booster injections. These reactions were characterized by erythema, induration and pruritus. These reactions eventually healed without any sustained reactions, eschar or scarring. None of the recipients experienced systemic reactions or widespread cutaneous eruptions.Intradermal injections of Mpox vaccine result in mild to moderate injection site reactions, most likely representing a vigorous cell‐mediated immune response. In all cases, the injection sites healed without complications.",Anthony A. Gaspari,10.1002/jvc2.282,https://doi.org/10.1002/jvc2.282,JEADV Clinical Practice,0,2023,no,The study does not indicate that it is focused on a population other than healthy adults. There is no mention of pregnancy or age groups under 18.,yes,"The study reports on adverse events, specifically injection site reactions.",yes,This is a case series of seven patients.,yes,The study involves human vaccine recipients.,no,"The paper does not state that it includes pregnant women, neonates, children, or adolescents; given the context of mpox vaccination in 2023, these recipients are likely adults.",no,"There is no evidence that participants received the vaccine during pregnancy, the neonatal period, childhood, or adolescence.",yes,The study involves the modern Mpox vaccine.,Exclude,"This case series of seven vaccine recipients focus on injection site reactions but does not include the target populations of interest such as pregnant women or children. Consequently, it fails the population-based inclusion criteria.","Population Focus, Target Population, Vaccination Timing",Target Population,0.1,"  - ""Seven recipients of the Mpox vaccine, administered via intradermal injection, were observed over time,""",,"  - ""All seven recipients experienced mild to moderate localized reactions to Mpox vaccine""",,"  - ""Seven recipients of the Mpox vaccine, administered via intradermal injection, were observed over time,""",,"  - ""Seven recipients of the Mpox vaccine, administered via intradermal injection, were observed over time,""",,"  - ""Seven recipients of the Mpox vaccine, administered via intradermal injection, were observed over time,""",,"  - ""Seven recipients of the Mpox vaccine, administered via intradermal injection, were observed over time,""",,"  - ""Seven recipients of the Mpox vaccine, administered via intradermal injection, were observed over time,""
