Comparison of Waning Antibody Responses After Natural Monkeypox Virus Infection and Mpox Vaccination Beyond 6 Months in South Korea,"Abstract Natural Monkeypox virus infection induced significantly higher neutralizing antibody titers than Jynneos vaccination, with similar antibody decay rates beyond 6 months. Jynneos recipients with prior smallpox vaccination showed antibody levels comparable to mpox convalescents.","So Yun Lim, Hyang Su Kim, Hong soon Yim, Hyesun Kim, In-Ae Han, Doran Yoon, Min-Kyung Kim, Yeonjae Kim, Jihye Um, Gayeon Kim, BumSik Chin, Jun-Sun Park, Jihwan Bang",10.1093/ofid/ofae566,https://doi.org/10.1093/ofid/ofae566,Open Forum Infectious Diseases,3,2024,no,The participants appear to be adults who recovered from mpox or were vaccinated; there is no evidence of non-adult or pregnant participants.,no,The study reports antibody titers and decay rates (immunogenicity) but does not report clinical safety outcomes or effectiveness outcomes such as prevention of infection.,yes,This is a primary research study comparing antibody responses between groups.,yes,The study involves human participants (convalescents and vaccine recipients).,no,"There is no mention of pregnant women, neonates, children, or adolescents as participants in the study.",yes,Participants with prior smallpox vaccination would have received the vaccine during childhood given the timeline of smallpox eradication and vaccine availability in South Korea.,yes,The study specifically evaluates Jynneos (an mpox vaccine) and historical smallpox vaccines.,Exclude,The study examines neutralizing antibody persistence in adults who had mpox or were vaccinated with Jynneos or historical smallpox vaccines. It fails the screening criteria because it does not include the target populations of children or pregnant women and focuses on immunogenicity rather than clinical outcomes of safety or effectiveness.,"Population Focus, Relevant Outcomes, Target Population",Target Population,0.1,"  - ""Natural Monkeypox virus infection induced significantly higher neutralizing antibody titers than Jynneos vaccination,""",,"  - ""Natural Monkeypox virus infection induced significantly higher neutralizing antibody titers than Jynneos vaccination,""",,"  - ""Natural Monkeypox virus infection induced significantly higher neutralizing antibody titers than Jynneos vaccination,""",,"  - ""Natural Monkeypox virus infection induced significantly higher neutralizing antibody titers than Jynneos vaccination,""
