Differences in Mpox and Vaccinia Immunity Induced by Non-Replicating and Replicating Vaccinia-Based Vaccines,"Background: The recent global outbreak with clade IIb and the concurrent emergence of clade I mpox virus in Africa show that mpox is a challenging problem. MVA-BN induces low-level mpox-neutralizing antibody responses that wane rapidly. This study was conducted to compare the mpox immunity induced by a replication-competent smallpox vaccine and non-replicating MVA-BN. Methods: Stored sera (n = 302) and PBMCs (n = 244) collected pre-vaccination and at five post-vaccination time points in MVA-BN and six post-vaccination time points in Dryvax clinical trials were used. Antibody titers that neutralized at least 50% of mpox in cell culture were determined by the focus reduction neutralization test (FRNT) 50, and the mpox-specific T cell responses were measured using an IFN-γ ELISPOT assay. Results: The peak geometric fold rise (95% CI) (i.e., the maximum GMFR across all study visits) in the mpox FRNT50 for subcutaneous (SC) MVA-BN, intradermal (ID) MVA-BN, and Dryvax was 22.1 (8.3, 59.1), 18.5 (8.0, 43.1), and 245.8 (100.4, 601.6), respectively. The GMFR at day 180 post-vaccination for MVA-BN (SC), MVA-BN (ID), and Dryvax was 2.4, 2.7, and 64, respectively. The mean (95% CI) peak number of mpox-specific IFN-γ-producing SFCs was 127 (43.1, 238.3), 87.3 (46, 137), and 61.2 (44.3, 77.7) for MVA-BN (SC), MVA-BN (ID), and Dryvax, respectively. On day 180, the mean SFCs in the three groups decreased to 10.8 (−34.4, 3.8), 3.3 (−6.2, 18.6), and 2.2 (−9, 12.5), respectively. Conclusions: The peak mpox-neutralizing antibody titer was >10-fold lower in MVA-BN recipients compared to those who received a replication-competent smallpox vaccine, and the level at day 180 was >20 times lower in MVA-BN recipients. MVA-BN induced similar or higher T cell responses.","G. Abate, Krystal A. Meza, Yinyi Yu, Chase Colbert, Anna Jaunarajs, Azra Blazevic, D. Hoft, S. Frey",10.3390/vaccines13050520,https://doi.org/10.3390/vaccines13050520,Vaccines,1,2025,no,"The study uses samples from existing clinical trials of MVA-BN and Dryvax. These trials are typically conducted in healthy adults, and there is no mention of pregnant women, children, or non-healthy populations in the abstract.",no,The study reports immunogenicity outcomes (neutralizing antibody titers and T cell responses) but does not report clinical effectiveness (prevention of infection) or safety outcomes (adverse events).,yes,The study appears to be a laboratory analysis using samples from previous clinical trials.,yes,The study uses human samples (sera and PBMCs).,no,"The background and methods do not indicate the inclusion of pregnant women, neonates, children, or adolescents.",no,"There is no evidence that vaccinations occurred during pregnancy, the neonatal period, or childhood/adolescence.",yes,"The study involves MVA-BN and Dryvax, which are vaccinia-based vaccines.",Exclude,This study is a laboratory analysis of immune responses (neutralizing antibodies and T cells) using samples from MVA-BN and Dryvax clinical trials. It fails multiple inclusion criteria because it does not study the target populations (pregnant women or children) and focuses on immunogenicity rather than clinical safety or effectiveness outcomes.,"Population Focus, Relevant Outcomes, Target Population, Vaccination Timing",Target Population,0.1,"  - ""Stored sera (n = 302) and PBMCs (n = 244) collected pre-vaccination and at five post-vaccination time points in MVA-BN and six post-vaccination time points in Dryvax clinical trials were used.""",,"  - ""Antibody titers that neutralized at least 50% of mpox in cell culture were determined by the focus reduction neutralization test (FRNT) 50, and the mpox-specific T cell responses were measured using an IFN-γ ELISPOT assay.""",,"  - ""Stored sera (n = 302) and PBMCs (n = 244) collected pre-vaccination and at five post-vaccination time points in MVA-BN and six post-vaccination time points in Dryvax clinical trials were used.""",,"  - ""Stored sera (n = 302) and PBMCs (n = 244) collected pre-vaccination and at five post-vaccination time points in MVA-BN and six post-vaccination time points in Dryvax clinical trials were used.""",,"  - ""This study was conducted to compare the mpox immunity induced by a replication-competent smallpox vaccine and non-replicating MVA-BN.""
