PRENATAL VACCINIA,"I u the past pregnancy has not been considered a contra-indication to vaccination. Because of the deadly course of smallpox in pregnant women, these were often the first to be vaccinated. However, most obstetricians now recognize the risk of fetal vaccinia and limit vaccination during pregnancy to those cases in which there has been direct exposure to smallpox (Abramowitz, 1957; Zellweger, 1957; Lyon, 1958). In eight cases (Lynch, 1932; McDonald and McArthur, 1952; Wiersum, 1956; Wielenga et a/., 1961; Tucker and Sibson, 1962; Entwistle et al., 1962; Naidoo and Hirsch, 1963; Hood and McKinnon, 1963) unequivocal fetal infection with vaccinia virus has been reported. In all these cases the mother had an acute febrile reaction to vaccination, and the fetus showed a generalized vaccinia eruption. In each case the virus was found in the fetus, or its presence established by histological discovery of inclusion bodies (Table I ) .","Gian Töundury, Mathias Foukas, Anthony Scouteris",10.1111/j.1471-0528.1969.tb09449.x,https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1471-0528.1969.tb09449.x,British Journal of Obstetrics and Gynaecology,0,1969,yes,"The study focuses on vaccinating pregnant women and the resulting effects on the fetus, which is not a healthy non-pregnant adult population.",yes,The study reports on fetal vaccinia infection as a complication of maternal vaccination.,yes,The study appears to be a Review or Case Series discussing eight reported cases.,yes,The study describes human clinical cases involving pregnant women and fetuses.,yes,The study specifically includes pregnant women and the impacts on the fetus/neonates.,yes,The vaccination occurred during pregnancy.,yes,The paper discusses smallpox vaccination and vaccinia virus infection.,Include,"This paper examines fetal vaccinia following smallpox vaccination during pregnancy, reporting outcomes from eight specific cases. It provides direct evidence regarding the safety of vaccinia-based vaccines in a target population (pregnant women and fetuses).",,,5,"  - ""limit vaccination during pregnancy to those cases in which there has been direct exposure to smallpox""
