Neutralizing antibody titers induced by JYNNEOS vaccine in unrecognized previous mpox virus exposed individuals.,"vaccination protocol, organized the sample and data collection, and obtained the funding.P. P. was responsible for data management.F. C. analyzed data.A. B.","D. Moschese, Micol Bianchi, M. Cossu, F. Salari, A. Giacomelli, A. Rizzo, Samuel Lazzarin, Federico Sabaini, S. Nozza, D. Mileto, A. Gori, S. Antinori, M. Gismondo, G. Rizzardini",10.1093/cid/ciad412,https://doi.org/10.1093/cid/ciad412,Clinical Infectious Diseases,4,2023,yes,"The study involves individuals with prior mpox exposure, which means they are not 'healthy' naive subjects, thus it is not exclusively limited to healthy adults.",no,"The title reports 'Neutralizing antibody titers', which are immunogenicity outcomes; the study does not clearly report the required clinical safety or effectiveness outcomes such as prevention of infection, hospitalization, or death.",yes,The mentions of a 'vaccination protocol' and 'data collection' suggest a primary research study.,yes,The focus on 'individuals' and 'vaccination protocol' indicates a human study rather than an animal or laboratory-only study.,no,"The study mentions 'individuals' in a general infectious disease context without any specific reference to or inclusion of pregnant women, neonates, or children.",no,"There is no evidence that vaccinations were administered during pregnancy, the neonatal period, or childhood.",yes,"The study specifically investigates the JYNNEOS vaccine, which is a vaccinia-based mpox vaccine.",Exclude,The paper investigates antibody responses to the JYNNEOS vaccine in individuals previously exposed to mpox virus. It is excluded because it does not include target populations such as children or pregnant women and focuses on immunogenicity titers rather than the required safety or clinical effectiveness outcomes.,"Relevant Outcomes, Target Population, Vaccination Timing",Target Population,0.1,,,,,"  - ""vaccination prot