"Mpox vaccination routes: prevalence, correlates and adverse effects of subcutaneous versus intradermal vaccination at a mass vaccination clinic in Sydney, Australia","The Royal Prince Alfred Hospital Mpox Vaccination Clinic opened in response to the 2022 multicountry mpox outbreak. A total of 9500 vaccinations were administered intradermally and subcutaneously during the first 16 weeks of clinic operation. The rate of adverse events was 0.1%. Compared to people who received the vaccine intradermally, those who received it subcutaneously were more likely to be aged 30–39 years (P = 0.047), sexual partners of gay and bisexual men (P < 0.001), eligible for Medicare (P < 0.001) and born in the Philippines (P = 0.01) or Malaysia (P = 0.04).","Alisa Pollack, Winston Lo, Hanaho Imamura, Ian Caterson",10.1111/imj.16386,https://doi.org/10.1111/imj.16386,Internal medicine journal (Print),0,2024,no,"The study focuses on a general adult population, specifically mentioning individuals aged 30-39 years and sexual partners of gay and bisexual men. There is no evidence that the study includes groups other than healthy non-pregnant adults.",yes,The study reports on the rate of adverse events.,yes,This is a primary research study reporting data from a mass vaccination clinic.,yes,The study involves human participants vaccinated at a clinic.,no,"The study population is described as being aged 30-39 years and does not mention any pregnant women, neonates, children, or adolescents.",no,"The participants were adults at a mass vaccination clinic responding to a 2022 outbreak and were likely vaccinated as adults, not during childhood or pregnancy.",yes,The study involves mpox vaccination during the 2022 outbreak.,Exclude,"This study evaluates mpox vaccination routes and adverse effects in a clinic population that appears to be composed entirely of adults, specifically highlighting participants aged 30-39. Because it does not include the target populations of pregnant women, children, or adolescents, it fails the inclusion criteria.","Population Focus, Target Population, Vaccination Timing",Target Population,0.1,"  - ""those who received it subcutaneously were more likely to be aged 30–39 years""
