Is smallpox vaccination protective against human monkeypox?,"Human Monkeypox (HMPX) has been spreading to non-endemic countries rapidly during spring-summer 2022 through human-to-human transmission, involving thousands of people, mostly men-who-have-sex-with-men. Little is known about the degree of protection due to previous smallpox vaccination. The cases described in our series show a mild clinical presentation of HMPX in those previously vaccinated. Our data are encouraging, and further investigations may lead to a fast public health prevention strategy. This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved.","D. Moschese, D. Farinacci, G. Pozza, A. Ciccullo, M. Cossu, A. Giacomelli, Fabio Borgonovo, D. Mileto, R. Santangelo, E. Tamburrini, G. Rizzardini, S. Antinori, S. Di Giambenedetto",10.1002/jmv.28077,https://doi.org/10.1002/jmv.28077,Journal of Medical Virology,10,2022,yes,"The study involves participants with monkeypox infection, meaning it is not limited to healthy individuals.",yes,The study reports on the clinical presentation and protection (effectiveness) against human monkeypox.,yes,The study is a case series as indicated by the mention of 'cases described in our series'.,yes,The study involves human cases of monkeypox.,no,"The population is described as mostly men-who-have-sex-with-men, and there is no evidence that pregnant women, neonates, children, or adolescents were included.",maybe,"While 'previous smallpox vaccination' likely occurred during childhood for this demographic, the study does not specifically analyze the timing for a pediatric or pregnant target population as required by criterion 5.",yes,The study assesses the effects of 'previous smallpox vaccination'.,Exclude,"The paper describes clinical outcomes for a series of human monkeypox patients who had received previous smallpox vaccination. It fails the primary screening because the study population consists primarily of men-who-have-sex-with-men and does not include the target groups of pregnant women, neonates, or pediatric participants.",Target Population,Target Population,0.1,"  - ""cases described in our series show a mild clinical presentation of HMPX""",,"  - ""cases described in our series show a mild clinical presentation of HMPX""
