Vaccination effects on reducing COVID‐19 complications in pregnancy: A large‐scale report from Iran,The objective of this study was to evaluate the effects of maternal coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID‐19) vaccination on preventing severe complications of COVID‐19 in pregnant women.,"N. Changizi, B. Eshrati, M. Salehi, M. Beheshtian, Leila Hadipour Jahromy, Nehzat Emami Afshar, Saeideh Hejazi, Sedigheh Hantoushzadeh, L. Eslamian, Mohsen Savaie, A. Raeisi, P. Pooransari",10.1002/ijgo.15077,https://doi.org/10.1002/ijgo.15077,International journal of gynaecology and obstetrics: the official organ of the International Federation of Gynaecology and Obstetrics,6,2023,yes,"The study focuses on pregnant women, meaning it is not limited to healthy non-pregnant adults.",no,"The study reports outcomes related to COVID-19 complications rather than mpox infection, hospitalization, or death.",yes,"The paper is a large-scale report, indicative of a primary research study.",yes,The study involves human participants (pregnant women).,yes,The study specifically includes pregnant women.,yes,Participants received the vaccine during pregnancy.,no,"The study evaluates COVID-19 vaccines, not vaccinia-based mpox or historical smallpox vaccines.",Exclude,"This study evaluates the effects of COVID-19 vaccination on severe complications in pregnant women. It is excluded because it does not involve vaccinia-based mpox or smallpox vaccines, and it does not report on mpox-related outcomes.","Relevant Outcomes, Vaccine Type",Vaccine Type,0.1,"  - ""evaluate the effects of maternal coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID‐19) vaccination on preventing severe complications of COVID‐19 in pregnant women.""",,"  - ""evaluate the effects of maternal coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID‐19) vaccination on preventing severe complications of COVID‐19 in pregnant women.""",,"  - ""evaluate the effects of maternal coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID‐19) vaccination on preventing severe complications of COVID‐19 in pregnant wo