The association between coronavirus disease 2019 vaccination during pregnancy and neonatal health outcomes,"Pregnant women have a higher risk of severe illness or complications due to a severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 infection. To reduce these risks, pregnant women are advised to coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID‐19) vaccination. Continued monitoring of the safety of maternal COVID‐19 vaccination remains important.","P. Woestenberg, Veronique Y F Maas, L. C. Vissers, Nadia M B Oliveri, Agnes C. Kant, Maud de Feijter",10.1002/ped4.12456,https://doi.org/10.1002/ped4.12456,Pediatric Investigation,3,2024,yes,The study focuses on pregnant women.,yes,The study monitors the safety of maternal vaccination.,maybe,"The text describes monitoring safety, which suggests a primary research study format (e.g., cohort study), though the specific design is not explicitly stated in the snippet.",yes,"The focus is on pregnant women, indicating a human study.",yes,The study includes pregnant women.,yes,The study concerns vaccination during pregnancy.,no,"The study exclusively discusses COVID-19 vaccines, not vaccinia-based mpox or historical smallpox vaccines.",Exclude,"While the study focuses on a target population (pregnant women) vaccinated during pregnancy, it investigates COVID-19 vaccines rather than the required vaccinia-based mpox or smallpox vaccines. Consequently, it does not meet the vaccine type inclusion criterion.",Vaccine Type,Vaccine Type,0.1,"  - ""pregnant women are advised to coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID‐19) vaccination.""",,"  - ""Continued monitoring of the safety of maternal COVID‐19 vaccination remains important.""",,,,"  - ""pregnant women are advised to coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID‐19) vaccination.""",,"  - ""pregnant women are advised to coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID‐19) vaccination.""",,"  - ""pregnant women are advised to coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID‐19) vaccination.""",,"  - ""pregnant women are advised to coronavirus disease 2019 