"Smallpox vaccination: a review, part II. Adverse events.","Smallpox vaccination of health care workers, military personnel, and some first responders has begun in the United States in 2002-2003 as one aspect of biopreparedness. Full understanding of the spectrum of adverse events and of their cause, frequency, identification, prevention, and treatment is imperative. This article describes known and suspected adverse events occurring after smallpox vaccination.","V. Fulginiti, A. Papier, J. Lane, John M. Neff, John M. Neff, D. Henderson",10.1086/375825,https://doi.org/10.1086/375825,Clinical Infectious Diseases,214,2003,maybe,"The abstract mentions vaccination of health care workers and military personnel, who are typically adults, but does not explicitly exclude non-healthy individuals or describe the full scope of the review population.",yes,The study focuses specifically on adverse events following vaccination.,maybe,The title identifies this as a review. It is unclear if it is a systematic review or a narrative review based on the limited abstract.,yes,The study describes clinical adverse events in human populations such as health care workers.,maybe,"The abstract mentions health care workers and military personnel, which are adult populations. There is no mention of pregnant women, neonates, or children in the abstract.",maybe,The timing of vaccination for the target groups (pregnant women/children) is not specified in the abstract.,yes,The study explicitly involves the smallpox vaccine.,Include,"This article is a review focusing on adverse events following smallpox vaccination in populations including health care workers and military personnel. While it clearly addresses relevant safety outcomes and vaccine types, the abstract does not specify whether the review includes data on pregnant women or children, requiring a full-text review to confirm eligibility.",,,3.6,"  - ""Smallpox vaccination of health care workers, military personnel, and some first responders has begun in the United States""",,"  - ""This article describes known and suspected adverse events occurring after smallpox vaccination.""",,,,"  - ""Smallpox vaccination of health care workers, military personnel, and some first responders has begun in the United States""
