Sequential Safety Surveillance of RSVpreF Vaccination During Pregnancy Early in the Postapproval Period,"This cohort study assesses the risk and incidence of preterm birth, pregnancy-associated hypertensive disorders, and other outcomes associated with an approved vaccine for respiratory syncytial virus administered during pregnancy.","Ashley I Michnick, Sarah C. MacDonald, S. Adimadhyam, Fang Zhang, A. Cosgrove, Andrew B Petrone, Katherine E Round, Sampada Gandhi, Nana Koram, O. E. Anastasiou, Heather Rubino, M. Lino, D. Djibo, Jennifer L. Kuntz, Shelly-Ann M. Love, Cheryl N. McMahill-Walraven, K. Palmsten, A. Wentz, Susan E. Andrade, Richard Platt, Judith C. Maro",10.1001/jamanetworkopen.2026.6190,https://doi.org/10.1001/jamanetworkopen.2026.6190,JAMA Network Open,1,2026,yes,"The study focuses on pregnant women, not exclusively healthy non-pregnant adults.",yes,The study reports safety outcomes including preterm birth and hypertensive disorders.,yes,This is described as a cohort study.,yes,The study tracks outcomes in a cohort of pregnant women.,yes,The study specifically includes pregnant women.,yes,The vaccine was administered during pregnancy.,no,"The study investigates the RSVpreF vaccine for respiratory syncytial virus, not a vaccinia-based mpox or historical smallpox vaccine.",Exclude,"While the study focuses on a target population (pregnant women) receiving a vaccine during pregnancy, it evaluates an RSV vaccine rather than an mpox or smallpox vaccine. Consequently, it does not meet the specified vaccine type criteria.",Vaccine Type,Vaccine Type,0.1,"  - ""vaccine for respiratory syncytial virus administered during pregnancy.""",,"  - ""This cohort study assesses the risk and incidence of preterm birth, pregnancy-associated hypertensive disorders, and other outcomes""",,"  - ""This cohort study assesses the risk and incidence of preterm birth, pregnancy-associated hypertensive disorders, and other outcomes""",,"  - ""This cohort study assesses the risk and 