  - ""These findings indicate potential broader benefits of HPV vaccination than have been documented to date.""",,"  - ""Using data from the National Perinatal Data Collection we compared rates of preterm births and small-for-gestational-age infants born in Australia 2000-2015.""",,"  - ""Using data from the National Perinatal Data Collection we compared rates of preterm births and small-for-gestational-age infants born in Australia 2000-2015.""",,"  - ""Using data from the National Perinatal Data Collection we compared rates of preterm births and small-for-gestational-age infants born in Australia 2000-2015.""",,"  - ""Publicly funded HPV vaccination of female adolescents began in Australia in 2007 with initial catch-up to age 26 years.""",,"  - ""Human papillomavirus (HPV) infection, and its sequelae of precancerous cervical lesions and their subsequent treatment, have been linked with an increased risk of adverse pregnancy outcomes.""
