Patent profile for the approved and in clinical trials Mpox vaccines.,"Mpox disease was reported in 110 countries since May 2022, with 88,026 cases and 148 deaths by 21 June 2023. Although some drugs were already approved for Mpox treatment, the available smallpox vaccines can provide 85% cross-prevention, but there are no scientific publications describing the patent portfolio for Mpox vaccines. This paper aims to contribute to the identification of the status of the smallpox vaccine patents now applied for Mpox. We retrieved ten vaccines, but only a few had a patent portfolio and one under patent litigation processes in three continents. Also, no specific Mpox vaccine was retrieved and, in this sense, technological monitoring studies should be performed to provide a future vision regarding Mpox prophylaxis.","Irene von der Weid, Cristina d'Urso de Souza Mendes, P. C. Fonseca, Sandro G Viveiros Rosa",10.4155/ppa-2023-0017,https://doi.org/10.4155/ppa-2023-0017,Pharmaceutical Patent Analyst,1,2023,no,The study is a patent profile analysis and does not involve a study population of human subjects.,no,The study focuses on patent status and litigation rather than clinical safety or effectiveness outcomes.,no,"This is a patent landscape or technological monitoring study, not a primary research study (like a cohort or RCT) or a clinical evidence synthesis.",no,"The study is a review of patent portfolios and legal statuses, not a human clinical study.",no,"The study does not include any human participants and therefore does not target pregnant women, neonates, or children.",no,No vaccinations were administered as part of this patent review.,yes,The study does involve smallpox vaccines applied for Mpox.,Exclude,"This study is a patent landscape analysis focused on the legal and intellectual property status of smallpox vaccines. It does not involve human participants, clinical outcomes, or relevant primary research designs, failing multiple inclusion criteria.","Population Focus, Relevant Outcomes, Study Design, Study Type, Target Population, Vaccination Timing",Study Type,0.1,"  - ""This paper aims to contribute to the identification of the status of the smallpox vaccine patents now applied for Mpox.""",,"  - ""This paper aims to contribute to the identification of the status of the smallpox vaccine patents now applied for Mpox.""
