The US smallpox vaccination program: a review of a large modern era smallpox vaccination implementation program.,"We describe the US experience with a large-scale smallpox vaccination program in the modern era and quantify the anticipated and unanticipated local and systemic side-effects of smallpox vaccination. In addition, we review unexpected issues, such as the development of myopericarditis discovered during the implementation of this program. These results constitute the largest dataset of a vaccinia vaccination program utilizing calf-lymph derived New York City Board of Health strain vaccine (Dryvax, Wyeth) since the 1970s. These results should inform current and future vaccinia vaccination programs and provide a historical rate of complications against which candidate vaccine side-effects can be compared in future clinical trials.","G. Poland, J. Grabenstein, J. Neff",10.1016/J.VACCINE.2005.01.012,https://doi.org/10.1016/J.VACCINE.2005.01.012,Vaccine,123,2005,no,"The study describes the modern era US smallpox vaccination program, which was restricted to military and healthcare workers, thus it was exclusively limited to healthy non-pregnant adults.",yes,The study reports on local and systemic side-effects and complications like myopericarditis.,yes,"The study is a review and description of program implementation results, meeting the design criteria.",yes,The study describes the vaccination program implementation in the US human population.,no,"The program described was conducted for military and first responders in the modern era, populations that did not include pregnant women, neonates, children, or adolescents.",no,"As the program was restricted to adults (military and healthcare workers), participants did not receive the vaccine during pregnancy, childhood, or adolescence.",yes,The study utilizes the vaccinia-based Dryvax vaccine.,Exclude,"The paper provides a review of safety outcomes from the modern era US smallpox vaccination program using the Dryvax vaccine. Because this program was specifically targeted at adult military and emergency personnel, it does not include the required populations of children, neonates, or pregnant women.","Population Focus, Target Population, Vaccination Timing",Target Population,0.1,"  - ""describe the US experience with a large-scale smallpox vaccination program in the modern era""",,"  - ""quantify the anticipated and unanticipated local and systemic side-effects of smallpox vaccination.""
