"Mpox in Children and Adolescents during Multicountry Outbreak, 2022–2023",The 2022–2023 mpox outbreak predominantly affected adult men; 1.3% of reported cases were in children and adolescents <18 years of age. Analysis of global surveillance data showed 1 hospital intensive care unit admission and 0 deaths in that age group. Transmission routes and clinical manifestations varied across age subgroups.,"Ana Hoxha, S. Kerr, Henry Laurenson-Schafer, Nikola Sklenovská, B. B. Mirembe, I. Nezu, P. Ndumbi, J. Fitzner, M. Almiron, M. Vila, R. Pebody, Aisling M Vaughan, J. Haussig, Luís Alves de Sousa, O. Lukoya, O. Sanni, P. Nabeth, Jeremias D Naiene, M. Kato, T. Matsui, Krutika Kuppalli, P. Mala, Rosamund F. Lewis, Olivier le Polain de Waroux, B. Pavlin",10.3201/eid2910.230516,https://doi.org/10.3201/eid2910.230516,Emerging Infectious Diseases,10,2023,yes,The study focus includes children and adolescents under 18 years of age.,yes,The study reports on clinical outcomes including ICU admissions and deaths.,yes,"The study is an analysis of global surveillance data, which fits within primary research (cohort/cross-sectional) or evidence synthesis.",yes,The study involves human case data from global surveillance.,yes,The study explicitly includes children and adolescents <18 years.,no,There is no mention of participants receiving a vaccine in the abstract provided.,no,The abstract does not mention vaccinia-based vaccines or historical smallpox vaccines; it focuses on clinical manifestations and surveillance of cases.,Exclude,"This study analyzes clinical surveillance data for mpox in children and adolescents, reporting on outcomes such as ICU admission and mortality. However, it fails the inclusion criteria because it does not evaluate vaccination or vaccine-related outcomes.","Vaccination Timing, Vaccine Type",Vaccination Timing,0.1,"  - ""1.3% of reported cases were in children and adolescents <18 years of age.""",,"  - ""Analysis of global surveillance data showed 1 hospital intensive care unit admission and 0 deaths in that age group.""",,"  - ""Analysis of global surveillance data showed 1 hospital intensive care unit admission and 0 deaths in that age group.""",,"  - ""1.3% of reported cases were in children and adolescents <18 years of age.""",,"  - ""1.3% of reported cases were in children and adolescents <18 years of age.""",,,,"  - ""Analysis of global surveillance data showed 1 hospital intensive care unit admission and 0 deaths in that age group.""
