Pregnancy Characteristics and Birth Outcomes in People with Mpox Infection During Pregnancy – Surveillance for Emerging Threats to Pregnant People and Infants Network,"We describe pregnancy characteristics among pregnant or recently pregnant people with laboratory confirmed or probable mpox infection during pregnancy and whose data were reported to CDC as of February 28, 2023. Infant characteristics are also reported among pregnancies resulting in a live birth.","Neelam V, Olsen E, Roth N, Newton S, Galang R, Hufstetler K, Zilversmit Pao L, Peterson B, Bachmann L, Tong V, Meaney-Delman D, Ellington S",10.1016/j.ajog.2023.09.025,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ajog.2023.09.025,American Journal of Obstetrics and Gynecology,1,2024,yes,"The study specifically focuses on pregnant and recently pregnant people, not exclusively healthy non-pregnant adults.",no,"While the study reports outcomes related to mpox infection (birth outcomes and patient characteristics), it does not report safety or effectiveness outcomes related to a vaccine.",yes,The study is a primary research report describing surveillance data reported to the CDC.,yes,The study involves human participants (pregnant people and infants).,yes,The study population consists of pregnant women and neonates/infants.,no,There is no mention of participants receiving a vaccine during pregnancy or any other period; the focus is on mpox infection.,no,The study evaluates mpox infection during pregnancy but does not involve or mention any vaccinia-based or historical smallpox vaccines.,Exclude,The study describes the characteristics and birth outcomes of individuals with mpox infection during pregnancy. It fails multiple inclusion criteria because it does not involve the administration of any mpox or smallpox vaccines.,"Relevant Outcomes, Vaccination Timing, Vaccine Type",Vaccine Type,0.1,"  - ""pregnant or recently pregnant people with laboratory confirmed or probable mpox infection during pregnancy""",,"  - ""pregnant or recent