HIV and mpox: evaluation of clinical course and outcomes from an international dermatologic registry.,"To the Editor: In July 2022, the World Health Organization declared ""mpox"" a public health emergency. Since outbreak onset, >91,000 cases have been reported. 1 CDC. 2022 Monkeypox Outbreak Global Map. 2022. https://www.cdc.gov/poxvirus/monkeypox/response/2022/world-map.htmlDate accessed: November 6, 2022 Google Scholar During the 2022 mpox outbreak, most disease courses were mild. 2 Yon H. Shin H. Shin J.I. et al. Clinical manifestations of human Mpox infection: a systematic review and meta-analysis. Rev Med Virol. 2023; 33e2446https://doi.org/10.1002/rmv.2446 Crossref Scopus (12) Google Scholar In some cases, however, severe outcomes were reported and included hospitalization and death. People living with HIV/AIDS (PLWH) have been disproportionally affected, and all immunocompromised individuals are at a higher risk of severe outcomes. 3 Mitjà O. Alemany A. Marks M. et al. Mpox in people with advanced HIV infection: a global case series. Lancet. 2023; 401: 939-949https://doi.org/10.1016/s0140-6736(23)00273-85 Crossref PubMed Scopus (0) Google Scholar ,4 Benites-Zapata V.A. Ulloque-Badaracco J.R. Alarcon-Braga E.A. et al. Clinical features, hospitalisation and deaths associated with monkeypox: a systematic review and meta-analysis. Ann Clin Microbiol Antimicrob. 2022; 21: 36https://doi.org/10.1186/s12941-022-00527-1 Crossref PubMed Scopus (86) Google Scholar Hospitalization in those diagnosed with mpox ranges from 14% to 59%. 4 Benites-Zapata V.A. Ulloque-Badaracco J.R. Alarcon-Braga E.A. et al. Clinical features, hospitalisation and deaths associated with monkeypox: a systematic review and meta-analysis. Ann Clin Microbiol Antimicrob. 2022; 21: 36https://doi.org/10.1186/s12941-022-00527-1 Crossref PubMed Scopus (86) Google Scholar In cases requiring hospitalization, death was reported in 4% of the cases, but it is as high as 25% in PLWH. 3 Mitjà O. Alemany A. Marks M. et al. Mpox in people with advanced HIV infection: a global case series. Lancet. 2023; 401: 939-949https://doi.org/10.1016/s0140-6736(23)00273-85 Crossref PubMed Scopus (0) Google Scholar ,4 Benites-Zapata V.A. Ulloque-Badaracco J.R. Alarcon-Braga E.A. et al. Clinical features, hospitalisation and deaths associated with monkeypox: a systematic review and meta-analysis. Ann Clin Microbiol Antimicrob. 2022; 21: 36https://doi.org/10.1186/s12941-022-00527-1 Crossref PubMed Scopus (86) Google Scholar Reports of dermatologic findings and associated clinical outcomes in PLWH are limited.","A. Strahan, Cristina Galvan Casas, S. Prasad, L. C. Fuller, K. Peebles, A. Carugno, K. Leslie, Joanna L Harp, Teodora Pumnea, D. McMahon, M. Rosenbach, J. Lubov, Geoffrey Chen, Ann Pacheco, L. Fox, Allen McMillen, Henry W Lim, A. Stratigos, Terrence A. Cronin, Mark D. Kaufmann, G. Hruza, Lars E. French, E. Freeman",10.1016/j.jaad.2023.12.032,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jaad.2023.12.032,Journal of American Academy of Dermatology,2,2023,yes,"The study focuses on people living with HIV/AIDS (PLWH) and immunocompromised individuals, which means it is not exclusively limited to healthy adults.",yes,The study explicitly mentions severe outcomes including hospitalization and death.,yes,"The study is an evaluation of data from an international dermatologic registry, which constitutes primary research (cohort study or case series).",yes,The study involves human clinical data from patient registries.,no,"The provided text discusses people living with HIV/AIDS but does not mention the inclusion of pregnant women, neonates, children, or adolescents.",no,The study evaluates the 'clinical course and outcomes' of mpox infection rather than vaccination; there is no mention of participants receiving vaccines during the specified vulnerable periods.,no,The study does not involve or mention vaccinia-based or historical smallpox vaccines.,Exclude,"The paper focuses on the clinical course and mortality 