Effectiveness of a single dose of JYNNEOS vaccine in real world: A systematic review and meta‐analysis,"Mpox infection is a zoonotic illness that resembles smallpox. Vaccination is widely regarded as a vital effective method of preventing mpox, however, there is lack of consensus of effectiveness of a single dose of mpox vaccine in the current 2022–2023 outbreak. We pooled data from real‐world studies to evaluate the efficacy of the JYNNEOS vaccination given as a single dosage.","A. M. Taha, A. M. Mahmoud, Khaled Abouelmagd, Sara Adel Abdelkader Saed, B. Khalefa, Sangam Shah, Prakasini Satapathy, M. A. Shamim, S. Sah, H. A. Serhan, Suzanne Donovan, Ranjit Sah, J. J. Barboza",10.1002/hsr2.70069,https://doi.org/10.1002/hsr2.70069,Health Science Reports,6,2024,maybe,"The abstract examines the '2022-2023 outbreak' through 'real-world studies', but does not explicitly state if the populations were exclusively limited to healthy non-pregnant adults.",yes,The study aims to 'evaluate the efficacy of the JYNNEOS vaccination'.,yes,The study is explicitly described as a 'systematic review and meta‐analysis'.,yes,"The pooled data comes from 'real‐world studies' regarding an 'outbreak', which indicates a human study.",maybe,"The provided text does not mention whether 'pregnant women, neonates, children, or adolescents' were included in the meta-analysis.",maybe,"There is no information regarding the timing of vaccination (e.g., childhood or pregnancy) for the 'single dosage' investigated.",yes,"The study evaluates the 'JYNNEOS vaccination', which is a vaccinia-based vaccine.",Include,"This paper is a systematic review and meta-analysis focused on the real-world effectiveness of the JYNNEOS vaccine during the 2022-2023 mpox outbreak. However, it remains unclear if the included real-world studies covered the specific target populations of children, adolescents, or pregnant women required by the inclusion criteria.",,,3.6,"  - ""current 2022–2023 outbreak.""
